1
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:07,423
Yeah.

2
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:08,674
RINRIN (20)
HOSTESS

3
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,801
It's tough. Mmm.

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,137
Hmm?

5
00:00:13,304 --> 00:00:17,308
TAI-CHAN (22)
HAIRSTYLIST

6
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:21,938
It's okay.

7
00:00:22,939 --> 00:00:26,525
Rinrin, do you want to go back
to the girls' room? All right. Let's go.

8
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,027
Thanks so much for talking to me.

9
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:30,196
- <i>He's so kind.</i>
- <i>That's friendship.</i>

10
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,281
- All right. Okay.
- Thank you.

11
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:33,658
Thank you.

12
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:52,761
KAMAKEN (30)
MMA FIGHTER/BUSINESS OWNER

13
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,523
Rinrin, let's talk.

14
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:10,028
I'll wait in the classroom.

15
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:18,745
I'm sorry about everything.

16
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:28,922
You know,

17
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,633
the fact is, up until now,

18
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:37,597
you're the one that I've been spending
all my time hanging out with.

19
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:40,600
And I do like you a lot.

20
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:47,398
Honestly, it caught me off guard
to hear Mimi say that.

21
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:48,942
But, you know,

22
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:51,861
I thought this through.

23
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:53,738
And I…

24
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,407
want to be with you.

25
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:02,371
I don't know how to put it,
but from my perspective,

26
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:04,206
I wish you'd thought about this more.

27
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:07,085
- I did. That's why we're talking now.
- That's not what I meant.

28
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:09,629
And besides, I…

29
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:12,549
never said my feelings wavered.

30
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:17,845
I was just surprised.
And I didn't want to hide it from you.

31
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:19,681
No, you said that you like her.

32
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,733
If we're going to be together,
after we leave here…

33
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:32,694
How do I put this? Like…

34
00:02:34,195 --> 00:02:36,905
Let's say you're back home
and out having drinks

35
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:38,740
and talking to a girl there.

36
00:02:38,741 --> 00:02:42,536
If she tells you she likes you,
your feelings might waver again.

37
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:44,664
And that's what made me unsure about us.

38
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:48,293
Come on. Why would you think that?

39
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:54,548
I've had so much fun
spending time with you.

40
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:57,217
There are things
that I've only shared with you.

41
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:58,386
You're special to me.

42
00:02:58,887 --> 00:02:59,846
And so…

43
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:02,974
I want you to know,
it's not what you think.

44
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:07,562
Like, she did tell me to talk to her more,
but I wouldn't go out of my way

45
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:11,148
to, like, invite Mimi
to come chat with me or anything.

46
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:12,816
- Okay.
- Right.

47
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:15,862
So, you know,
I don't want you to get the wrong idea.

48
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,281
Please don't say you'll drop out.

49
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:27,206
It looks like Rinrin
just can't forgive him anymore, right?

50
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:28,916
- I want her to forgive him.
- Mmm.

51
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:29,834
NAGANO

52
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:39,385
Well, if it isn't Kamaken.

53
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,429
- Hey there.
- Hi there.

54
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:43,931
I didn't know there was a bench.

55
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,599
- It's always been here.
- Hmm?

56
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,143
- It's been here.
- There we go.

57
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:50,187
- I'm sitting next to you, if that's okay.
- Go ahead.

58
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,314
Oh, nice.

59
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:56,026
At first, I didn't think
you were interested in me.

60
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:58,071
- I convinced myself you weren't.
- Mmm.

61
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,530
- You're impossible to read.
- No, I'm not.

62
00:04:00,531 --> 00:04:02,449
- You are.
- But you know, in relationships,

63
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:05,869
I'm usually not the one to make
the first move or approach someone.

64
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:07,913
- I guessed that much.
- I tend to go for a safer option.

65
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:10,041
- To be honest, I think it comes down to…
- Right.

66
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:12,793
…some trauma from being cheated on
in a past relationship.

67
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:14,795
- Wait, that happened?
- Yeah.

68
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:18,924
If it weren't for him cheating on me,
I probably wouldn't have become a hostess.

69
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:20,342
- Wow.
- I was so mad at men.

70
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,344
- Like, "Screw them!" You know?
- Yeah. Right.

71
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:25,515
Like, "I'll just take
all the money I can from men!"

72
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,100
That's one reason I became a hostess.

73
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:30,769
Also for the money, because working
as a nursery school teacher

74
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:31,687
didn't pay enough.

75
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:32,729
Right, right.

76
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:36,024
So, I was like, "Oh, okay then,"
and started the hostess job.

77
00:04:36,025 --> 00:04:39,945
And since then, I don't go for a man
who doesn't show interest in me first.

78
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:42,406
I don't make any sort of move
until they make a move.

79
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:45,534
- Yeah, makes sense.
- So that's just a part of how I operate.

80
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:48,121
So it's hard for me
to initiate romantic connection.

81
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:51,873
But, you know, I mean…
How should I say it?

82
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:54,584
When I heard
that you were interested in me,

83
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:56,169
I regretted not making a move.

84
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:57,671
- Mmm-hmm.
- If I'm being honest.

85
00:04:57,672 --> 00:04:58,631
- Yeah.
- But…

86
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:02,467
I don't think it's right
to suddenly change my mind now.

87
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:03,303
Yeah.

88
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:07,264
So, yeah, I wanted to make sure
I shared that with you.

89
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:09,726
That's why I asked to chat now.

90
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,439
Seriously.

91
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:18,401
- It's tough being an old lady.
- It's tough being an old man.

92
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:21,194
- Good luck. Yeah.
- Okay, thanks.

93
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:23,196
- Say hi to Rinrin.
- Let me know if you need anything.

94
00:05:23,197 --> 00:05:24,573
- Yeah. Thank you.
- Yeah, bye.

95
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,450
- Bye-bye.
- <i>Well done, Kamaken.</i>

96
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,660
- <i>I admire that.</i>
- <i>Good job.</i>

97
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:30,954
<i>That was just
so incredibly thoughtful of him.</i>

98
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:31,998
<i>Yeah.</i>

99
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:46,636
- There we go.
- What's up? It's the last day.

100
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:49,097
- It's crazy, right?
- Yeah, it went by so fast.

101
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:50,015
SARA (26)
NAIL ARTIST

102
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:50,850
KAZUMA (26)
PART-TIMER

103
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:53,561
Oh, also, I finished the drawing.

104
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:55,104
Can I see it?

105
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,856
You said you like
sharp and vivid coloring,

106
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,191
so this is what I pictured.

107
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:01,109
Whoa.

108
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:02,194
Insane.

109
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:04,905
I had the feeling
that you might like these colors too.

110
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,656
- Yeah, I like them a lot.
- I thought so.

111
00:06:06,657 --> 00:06:09,076
It's super good. Yeah, that's crazy.

112
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:11,204
I can't believe you did this so quickly.

113
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:13,539
Amazing.

114
00:06:14,123 --> 00:06:18,168
I was thinking of you the whole time,
so it was easy to keep going.

115
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,629
Thank you so much. It's insane.

116
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,089
It's just incredible.

117
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:23,673
I want to keep growing as an artist,

118
00:06:23,674 --> 00:06:25,760
so I'd like to draw something
for you again.

119
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:29,471
And I could ink you
if I ever become a real tattoo artist.

120
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:31,015
Definitely. I'd like that.

121
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:34,644
- I'm looking forward to it. Wow.
- Me too.

122
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:37,938
But, you know, for me to be successful,
or even get better,

123
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:40,607
I think with you by my side,
I'd be able to work even harder.

124
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:41,983
Yeah, I guess so.

125
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:44,569
If I was there, I could cheer you on.

126
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,989
That's true. Of course.

127
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,952
Also, I feel like
I would make you my priority,

128
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,286
more than anyone else could.

129
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:55,330
- Mmm.
- And of all the guys here,

130
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:57,582
I'm the one who likes you the most,

131
00:06:57,583 --> 00:06:59,835
and I believe I can make you the happiest.

132
00:06:59,836 --> 00:07:01,712
That's why I've always been sincere,

133
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:06,426
and, you know, I've been gravitating
to you this whole time.

134
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,762
I'll put those feelings
into words tomorrow

135
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,264
and share them.

136
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:14,475
I'll also think deeply about it all.

137
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,770
And share my feelings with you.

138
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:20,398
Okay.

139
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:22,774
- Where's the middle?
- There.

140
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:23,901
- Here?
- Yeah.

141
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:28,488
- Whoa.
- Hey.

142
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:30,323
- Still talking? It's taking forever.
- No.

143
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:31,283
RYOPI (29)
BAR OWNER

144
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:35,078
- Of course. It's the last day.
- He's gonna write "Graduation."

145
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:36,830
- Wanna write it?
- Okay, sure.

146
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:38,665
Be right back. Gotta pee.

147
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:40,501
Just let me write this one.

148
00:07:50,636 --> 00:07:52,054
- There!
- Nice.

149
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:54,306
- How does it look?
- Looks good.

150
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:56,017
GRADUATION

151
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:01,272
- I told Sara how I feel, so no regrets.
- Yeah?

152
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:04,775
- I bet.
- Tomorrow's the day.

153
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:07,570
- The showdown?
- Yeah, the showdown.

154
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:10,072
Do your best.

155
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:15,035
- And you do the same.
- You're like, "Are you patronizing me?"

156
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:17,412
- You do your best too.
- Like, "How dare you interrupt us?"

157
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:20,040
You're damn right.
You surprised me, coming in like that.

158
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:22,752
I thought you were full of crap at first.

159
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,297
I mean, I also have my reasons, of course.

160
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:32,261
- We'll be proper men, right?
- Sure.

161
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,888
- You think you'll win?
- Piece of cake.

162
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:37,390
- Against the great me?
- No problem.

163
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:40,352
That's the spirit.
Otherwise, it's not worth the effort.

164
00:08:40,353 --> 00:08:42,020
Of course. I'm a real man.

165
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:43,813
<i>Oh, these two have a good relationship.</i>

166
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:45,607
<i>Yeah, their friendship is nice, right?</i>

167
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:46,775
- Okay.
- See ya.

168
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,068
Tomorrow, we're enemies.

169
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:50,695
Shut up. Just leave already, punk.

170
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:53,406
I'll knock you out. For real!

171
00:08:53,407 --> 00:08:55,076
I have no regrets at this point.

172
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,244
Because I was determined.

173
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:59,789
I only had eyes for Sara
for the past two weeks.

174
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:07,295
- I think you're the one I click most with.
- Oh. Why's that?

175
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:09,715
You know,
in terms of how effortless it is.

176
00:09:10,716 --> 00:09:13,218
Yeah, in the end, I don't know, it's like,

177
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:16,137
when I take everything
into account, it's you.

178
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:17,056
It has to be you.

179
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:19,058
Oh.

180
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:21,393
- Stop saying "Oh."
- No, I'm glad.

181
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:23,144
I am, I swear.

182
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:24,355
- It's nothing.
- Okay.

183
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:29,067
So, I'm thinking, like, I had a girlfriend
for about five years, you know?

184
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:30,819
- Right, you told me.
- Right, yeah.

185
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,488
- And being with her was too much trouble.
- Hmm.

186
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:36,116
But that relationship
was a serious one for me.

187
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,158
Mmm.

188
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:39,578
And now, I don't know
how to be in love like that anymore.

189
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,204
Right. Same here.

190
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:43,415
But then,
I guess it's okay if I don't know.

191
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:46,960
Like, if you fall in love too hard,
that can be trouble, right?

192
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,170
Yeah, you're right.

193
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:51,966
That's why I think it's okay
to keep a comfortable distance.

194
00:09:52,466 --> 00:09:54,759
And you're the person
who keeps the best distance from me.

195
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,636
- Is that a compliment?
- It's a compliment.

196
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:58,305
This is a compliment, for sure.

197
00:09:58,306 --> 00:10:01,016
Isn't it nice? Hassle-free is great.

198
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:02,601
- A comfortable distance?
- Yeah.

199
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:04,769
Well, I guess that's true.

200
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:05,895
- Yeah.
- Right.

201
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:10,525
That's why, taking all that into account,
I think you're the one for me.

202
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:11,610
You've got a point.

203
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:14,739
It's pretty amazing.
I think this resonated with me the most.

204
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,907
- Really?
- You're always making jokes.

205
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:18,825
Right?

206
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:21,661
- But I thought I'd be serious today.
- That's because it's the last day!

207
00:10:21,662 --> 00:10:23,247
- Yeah.
- It'd be bad if you didn't.

208
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:26,292
Right.

209
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,753
Let's see, how do I put it?

210
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:34,216
It's almost like
you're sharing your mind with someone?

211
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,551
The good and the bad.

212
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:38,303
And I realized that it's important

213
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,972
to communicate the good stuff
and the annoying stuff.

214
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:44,685
Yeah, and I was reminded once again
how I should cherish the moment

215
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,312
and focus on the present.

216
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:50,858
Even if she chooses Kazuma,
I won't have any regrets. None.

217
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:54,737
Yeah. Even if she picks Kazuma
or someone else, I'll be content.

218
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:58,616
I think I communicated that,
so I think I'm good.

219
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,995
Hmm. I'm having trouble choosing.

220
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:05,705
I'm not sure yet.

221
00:11:05,706 --> 00:11:07,749
Kazuma tells me

222
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:10,502
how he feels about me pretty directly.

223
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:12,796
But I've never heard Ryopi
share those feelings.

224
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:14,589
"I'm interested in you."

225
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:18,343
Or like, "Out of everyone here,
I'd choose you."

226
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:21,513
And that kind of makes me feel
like I'm just a leftover.

227
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:24,933
So there's a part of me that wonders
if he's being real.

228
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:28,269
So I want to hear how he truly feels
when he confesses.

229
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,773
If he's just still making jokes,
I might not choose him.

230
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:35,443
When they confess their feelings,
if either of them says the right things

231
00:11:35,444 --> 00:11:37,779
and convinces me
that they're the right guy for me,

232
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:41,241
then I might just trust my feelings
and choose in that moment.

233
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:44,161
But if I still can't shake
this feeling of uncertainty,

234
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:47,164
I might have to say no to both of them.

235
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:49,291
Yeah.

236
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:09,060
- So, she had some concerns.
- That came as a surprise, right?

237
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:10,979
- I thought she was set on Ryopi.
- Me too.

238
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:14,149
Yeah. They said they were
on the same wavelength.

239
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:18,278
But, come to think of it,
Ryopi hasn't said anything like,

240
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,780
"I have strong feelings for you,
and I'll be devoted to you."

241
00:12:20,781 --> 00:12:23,658
I was surprised that Sara actually wanted
to hear that from him.

242
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:26,536
- You're right, I totally agree.
- She wanted him to make it clear.

243
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:27,746
- Yeah.
- Right?

244
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,999
- That took me by surprise, honestly.
- Right?

245
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:33,042
Hey, you forgot your bag.

246
00:12:33,043 --> 00:12:34,419
- Oh, thank you.
- Here.

247
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,964
I thought I'd left it,
but I was going to go get it later.

248
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,966
- You're very kind.
- No worries.

249
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,217
KAHOCHI (20)
HOSTESS

250
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:43,262
- It's the last day.
- The last day.

251
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:45,306
So, you know, yesterday,

252
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:49,768
I was gonna ask you for a one-on-one
if I didn't have a fever.

253
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:50,685
Oh, yeah?

254
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:52,937
Yeah, but then you came
to the girls' room.

255
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:55,607
So, at that point,
I was glad I had a fever.

256
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:56,691
- For real?
- Yeah.

257
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:59,737
- So we could talk?
- Yeah. I was like, "Lucky me."

258
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:03,406
So, you were a transfer student,

259
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:05,241
- and you were only here for a week.
- Yeah.

260
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:06,911
But I wish I'd talked to you more

261
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,412
- while we had the time.
- Mmm.

262
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:11,414
Yeah, I felt the same way.

263
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:15,001
And that's why I feel like
if I had three more days,

264
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:16,961
I wouldn't have any regrets.

265
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:19,839
- So, you still have some regrets?
- Of course I do.

266
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:25,012
Because I decided to focus on you
just yesterday, or the day before.

267
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:28,431
- Seriously?
- Really.

268
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:30,017
Yeah, so…

269
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:32,936
You've liked Sara from day one, right?

270
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:37,316
I thought you were a very devoted
and sincere person.

271
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:40,527
And that kind of made me
like you even more.

272
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,986
- Oh, really?
- Yeah, yeah.

273
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:44,280
- That's nice to hear, you know.
- Yeah?

274
00:13:44,281 --> 00:13:46,324
I've never had a girl
catch feelings for me first.

275
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:47,283
Right, right.

276
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:49,119
- I've never been popular with girls.
- I see.

277
00:13:51,121 --> 00:13:53,749
So, like… How should I put it?

278
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:58,044
- When it's telling someone how I feel…
- Yeah.

279
00:13:58,045 --> 00:14:00,922
…it's easy, because I just have
to be honest with myself.

280
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:04,467
But, like, flirting and stuff,
getting someone to fall for me

281
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:05,552
- is not my thing.
- I see.

282
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:07,972
- Because I'm not very good with words.
- Makes sense.

283
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:11,140
- Yeah.
- But that's nice, you know?

284
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:13,726
- That awkward side of you. You know…
- You think so?

285
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:16,980
You're genuine and sincere,
and that's what I liked about you.

286
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,607
You're great the way you are.

287
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:25,864
- You know that…
- Yeah?

288
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,574
- …I have a kid?
- Sure.

289
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:30,034
- So, I think that you're amazing.
- Mmm.

290
00:14:30,035 --> 00:14:33,664
Because right now, my ex-wife
is in the same situation as you.

291
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:38,586
- And that is a tough spot to be in.
- Mmm-hmm.

292
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:42,922
Of course, it's only natural as a man
for me to support financially,

293
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:44,507
but that alone doesn't make me a good dad.

294
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:45,342
Right, yeah.

295
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,553
The only thing I can say to her is,

296
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:51,806
"I'm sorry for not being able
to be together with you."

297
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:55,227
That's why I'm really,
you know, super grateful

298
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:57,103
to my ex-wife for all she does.

299
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:57,938
Mmm-hmm.

300
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:00,190
- You're only 20, but still.
- Mmm.

301
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:01,900
I think it's so cool

302
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:04,027
that you're living your life
as a grown woman.

303
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,029
- Yeah.
- I do.

304
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,229
Hello there.

305
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:42,608
<i>Hi, Mom, how is it going?</i>

306
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,527
- Wow.
- <i>What are you doing?</i>

307
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:47,987
<i>I was drinking milk.</i>

308
00:15:47,988 --> 00:15:50,031
- You were drinking milk?
- <i>Yeah.</i>

309
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:53,201
You know,
Mommy has been learning a lot here.

310
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:55,286
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- You know what it means?

311
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:57,330
- <i>Uh-huh.</i>
- Yeah, so that means,

312
00:15:57,331 --> 00:16:00,042
once I come home,
Mommy's going to try extra hard.

313
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:03,628
<i>I'll wipe your tears.</i>

314
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:05,797
You'll wipe my tears? Thank you.

315
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:08,717
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- Remember, it's gonna be okay.

316
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:12,595
<i>It will, because I love you.</i>

317
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:14,722
Because you love me? Thank you.

318
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:15,891
I love you too.

319
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:17,976
Thank you so much

320
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,560
- for always wiping my tears.
- <i>Yeah.</i>

321
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:20,979
You're the best.

322
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:22,022
<i>It's okay.</i>

323
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:25,066
- You know, your mommy…
- <i>Yeah?</i>

324
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:28,111
…will do her best tomorrow,
and then she'll come home, okay?

325
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:30,655
<i>Okay. You can do it, Mommy.</i>

326
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,032
I can, right?

327
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,325
<i>I love you, Mommy.</i>

328
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:35,452
You love me?

329
00:16:36,453 --> 00:16:37,705
Thank you.

330
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:39,956
<i>Bye-bye!</i>

331
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:41,458
Bye-bye!

332
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,343
Well, even if he likes Sara more,

333
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:56,180
I want him to know
that I had a big crush on him

334
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:58,058
so that he can reflect on it later.

335
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:03,313
So, tomorrow at graduation, I'm going
to be completely honest with Kazuma

336
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:06,608
and tell him how I feel about him.

337
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:10,194
I know that I want to honor
my own feelings, but also,

338
00:17:10,195 --> 00:17:13,741
I want to be sure I honor the feelings
of someone who cares about me.

339
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:15,950
Even though Kahochi told me

340
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:18,704
that she just started
having these feelings for me,

341
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:23,250
they're still feelings
that I want to fully accept in my heart.

342
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:24,793
I'm not…

343
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:27,336
a super smart guy,

344
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:30,590
and there's still this person
who wants to be with me.

345
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:34,052
So her feelings are something
I definitely want to acknowledge.

346
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:36,930
I want to make sure
I take her feelings seriously.

347
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:52,904
You know, if Kahochi
hadn't shared these feelings with him,

348
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,447
Kazuma wouldn't be wavering.

349
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,450
- He's not that kind of a guy.
- Mmm.

350
00:17:57,451 --> 00:18:00,788
But if someone says something like that,
and you've never heard it before,

351
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:04,165
you're going to question things,
no matter how strong your feelings are.

352
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:05,416
- Right?
- I see.

353
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:07,376
So? How do you feel?

354
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:09,128
Be honest.

355
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:10,505
RUNE (28)
RAPPER/BUSINESS OWNER

356
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,132
- I imagine you're probably torn.
- Yeah.

357
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,219
Mmm, if I'm being honest…

358
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:21,975
there was a time when I thought
that I should stop thinking about you…

359
00:18:23,393 --> 00:18:24,436
for a while.

360
00:18:26,522 --> 00:18:29,858
But to me,
that felt like I was running away.

361
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:35,447
And a part of me was wondering
if it was okay to give up so quickly.

362
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:39,660
Truthfully, if you hadn't
joined our group…

363
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:45,541
I'm not sure I would have
ever fallen in love at all in this school.

364
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:48,626
- I feel the same way.
- Mmm.

365
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:51,004
- Mimi, I have strong feelings for you.
- Hmm.

366
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,842
I want to honor you and cherish you.

367
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,304
And I want to work hard for you
because of that.

368
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:01,056
Those feelings

369
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:03,600
are unlikely to change.

370
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:13,568
Whenever I'm in trouble,
you're always the one who helps me.

371
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,611
Mmm.

372
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:19,366
- Hmm. You know?
- Hmm.

373
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,043
Well, I've given her everything I've got,

374
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:33,588
and I left absolutely nothing
on the table.

375
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:37,426
I just gotta stay committed and be honest,
as I focus on Mimi.

376
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:40,137
I'll give it my all.

377
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:43,849
I hope I can make her smile,
and we both go home together.

378
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:50,271
I think up till now,
I've been a bit of a coward,

379
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,441
and I wasn't good at trusting people.

380
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:54,568
But they're so…

381
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:57,404
How should I put it?

382
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:02,575
I mean, I don't think
I've ever had the chance

383
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:06,830
to meet people who would pursue me
so directly and passionately.

384
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,789
And to be completely honest,

385
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:12,336
I still can't make up my mind
at this point.

386
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:16,715
Well, either I choose one of them,

387
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,052
or I don't choose any of them.

388
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:27,434
Hmm. I think it will have to be
one of those two choices.

389
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:32,021
Yeah. I mean, I still can't quite tell

390
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:34,148
if she even wants to choose
any of these three guys,

391
00:20:34,149 --> 00:20:35,901
- even though graduation is tomorrow.
- Yeah, yeah.

392
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:39,445
This victim mentality
that she's held on to

393
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:41,322
is something she needs to step out of.

394
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:43,115
- Otherwise, nothing will change.
- Yeah.

395
00:20:43,116 --> 00:20:45,409
- And isn't this a great opportunity?
- Right?

396
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:47,161
- To change at this school?
- Yeah.

397
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:49,664
Yeah, so, choosing someone…

398
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:51,415
- Yeah.
- …is a must.

399
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:52,959
I hope she chooses someone.

400
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,210
MARU (28)
HOST/PRESIDENT

401
00:20:54,211 --> 00:20:58,632
I've already decided on the girl
I want to confess to. Mmm.

402
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:03,929
That said, there's this girl
who has feelings for me,

403
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:07,140
and now I know
the depth of those feelings.

404
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:09,142
Mmm.

405
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:14,064
I don't know how I'll react
when I hear her confess.

406
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:19,361
Like, it's hard to predict
how I'm going to feel when that happens.

407
00:21:20,153 --> 00:21:22,030
I'm being totally real with you.

408
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:23,615
Yeah.

409
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:25,741
Tomorrow, I want to confess to Maru.

410
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:26,659
AYACHERU (24)
HOSTESS

411
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:30,162
Yeah. Well, I don't mind
if he rejects me, actually.

412
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:32,582
I mean, I think my chances are probably…

413
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:34,875
close to zero.

414
00:21:34,876 --> 00:21:37,796
But, okay, I'll just do
what I have to do, you know?

415
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:40,965
Maru was the one
I spent the most time with.

416
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:44,135
Like, we were together
from the beginning until the end.

417
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:46,387
So, when I think about it,

418
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:49,640
there's a part of me who wants
to tell him how grateful I am.

419
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:50,600
Yeah.

420
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:53,437
Hey.

421
00:21:55,230 --> 00:21:56,939
- I wanted to see you.
- Okay.

422
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,107
SHARAN (21)
LOUNGE HOSTESS

423
00:21:58,108 --> 00:22:01,402
So, like I said yesterday,
I've always liked you.

424
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:02,737
- Mmm-hmm.
- Yeah.

425
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,155
Your feelings are…

426
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:06,949
- I think you heard them loud and clear.
- 1,000%, yeah.

427
00:22:06,950 --> 00:22:08,868
- Yeah.
- They're crystal clear, for sure.

428
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:09,703
Right.

429
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:14,790
But there are times
when I feel like I don't know anymore.

430
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:16,043
Mmm.

431
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:19,755
I mean, you never know,
they might change again tonight.

432
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,093
- I mean…
- Yeah.

433
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:26,886
You know what?

434
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:29,388
You and I actually have
something in common.

435
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:30,932
- Mmm-hmm.
- Mmm.

436
00:22:31,808 --> 00:22:35,144
When we wanted to run away,
we faced it instead.

437
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:38,565
- Yeah, that's true. I did try to run away.
- Right? But you faced it.

438
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:41,400
- We're similar, aren't we?
- Mmm-hmm. Yeah.

439
00:22:41,401 --> 00:22:44,446
We are. I also wanted to run away. But…

440
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:48,616
I feel like both of us
changed at this school. For sure.

441
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:50,368
- A lot.
- So much.

442
00:22:50,369 --> 00:22:51,952
I can face things now.

443
00:22:51,953 --> 00:22:53,954
- Yeah.
- I gained that strength while I was here.

444
00:22:53,955 --> 00:22:55,664
- Hmm.
- For sure.

445
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,500
- I'll always remember this.
- Me too.

446
00:22:57,501 --> 00:22:58,626
- Forever.
- Forever.

447
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:02,171
Seriously. I'm super happy.

448
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:03,048
Yeah.

449
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:06,759
Tomorrow, we might have
to say goodbye to everyone.

450
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:09,763
No, no, I don't want to do that yet. Mmm.

451
00:23:10,305 --> 00:23:12,223
I'm not ready for that.

452
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:14,851
- I know.
- I really don't want to.

453
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:19,147
I like you so much, it hurts.
Seriously, so much.

454
00:23:20,565 --> 00:23:22,025
Oh no, I kissed you.

455
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:24,778
Jeez.

456
00:23:25,362 --> 00:23:26,363
Lift me up?

457
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,448
Sure, I can do that.

458
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:30,409
Oh!

459
00:23:34,621 --> 00:23:37,331
- This might be the last time, so…
- Yeah.

460
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:39,708
…I can be clingy.

461
00:23:39,709 --> 00:23:42,254
- I like you so much, Tai-chan.
- Mmm. Yeah.

462
00:23:44,798 --> 00:23:46,216
I feel blessed.

463
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:51,430
Like, hmm…

464
00:23:52,055 --> 00:23:55,850
There might be a chance,
so I have to believe in it and in myself.

465
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:57,935
- <i>Wow!</i>
- <i>She really changed.</i>

466
00:23:57,936 --> 00:24:02,315
When I talked to Sharan one last time,
my heart wavered for a moment.

467
00:24:04,651 --> 00:24:06,319
I mean, I wonder why.

468
00:24:09,823 --> 00:24:12,491
You know, this quote crossed my mind
in that moment.

469
00:24:12,492 --> 00:24:15,078
Something like,
"Love the woman that loves you."

470
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:17,788
Yeah.

471
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:20,499
- Whose quote is that?
- Who said that?

472
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,834
"Love the woman that loves you."

473
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:24,044
- What? Who was he quoting?
- Come on, who said that?

474
00:24:24,045 --> 00:24:25,588
Where did he hear something like that?

475
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:27,632
- What a selfish quote.
- Absolutely.

476
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:29,926
<i>Tonight is the last night.</i>

477
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:33,847
<i>Everyone, please gather
in the schoolyard now.</i>

478
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:39,852
- What is this?
- Wait, what are we looking at?

479
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:41,813
- What is this, seriously?
- Is it a magic show?

480
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:53,992
<i>It's the prime time of their life.</i>

481
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:19,725
<i>There's still one day left,
but up till now, we've given our all.</i>

482
00:25:19,726 --> 00:25:22,228
<i>We all worked together
to get to this moment.</i>

483
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:25,148
<i>And I'm proud of that.
Thank you for coming into my life.</i>

484
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:28,817
<i>I came here to find love,
but I ended up learning a lot of things,</i>

485
00:25:28,818 --> 00:25:30,361
<i>not just about romance.</i>

486
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:33,197
<i>We've all changed for the better
over the past two weeks.</i>

487
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:36,075
<i>I realized that it's okay to be myself.</i>

488
00:25:36,076 --> 00:25:40,330
<i>Spending time with you all
has taught me so much, for real.</i>

489
00:25:41,248 --> 00:25:44,000
<i>I don't know, like, seriously,</i>

490
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:47,962
<i>these have probably been
the most intense two weeks</i>

491
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:49,797
<i>of my entire life so far,</i>

492
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:51,633
<i>and I'm sure they always will be.</i>

493
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,242
Are those manly tears?

494
00:27:05,874 --> 00:27:07,207
<i>Hello?</i>

495
00:27:07,208 --> 00:27:09,127
- Oh, hello?
- <i>Hi.</i>

496
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:12,630
- Is this Bo?
- <i>Yeah. Been a while.</i>

497
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:14,423
Yeah, it has. How are you?

498
00:27:14,424 --> 00:27:16,175
<i>I'm doing good. What's up?</i>

499
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:19,928
- Yeah, so, like, Part 1 ended.
- <i>Right.</i>

500
00:27:19,929 --> 00:27:22,097
And then one of the Part 2 members

501
00:27:22,098 --> 00:27:23,642
gave me a baptism of fire.

502
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:26,268
<i>You show 'em what you got?</i>

503
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:28,937
Oh, you know, maybe just a little.

504
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:30,856
<i>Anyone there as good as me?</i>

505
00:27:30,857 --> 00:27:33,068
No way, no one can top you.

506
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:36,696
<i>You're right.</i>

507
00:27:37,614 --> 00:27:38,740
And, you know,

508
00:27:39,532 --> 00:27:42,701
somehow, I feel like
I've been a lot more myself in Part 2.

509
00:27:42,702 --> 00:27:43,619
But then…

510
00:27:43,620 --> 00:27:44,620
<i>Yeah?</i>

511
00:27:44,621 --> 00:27:47,581
Mmm, the ones that made me feel that way

512
00:27:47,582 --> 00:27:49,708
are the people I'd already met in Part 1.

513
00:27:49,709 --> 00:27:51,544
So, I'm super grateful for that.

514
00:27:53,421 --> 00:27:56,548
<i>If you feel that way,
that means you have grown a bit more.</i>

515
00:27:56,549 --> 00:27:57,384
Yeah.

516
00:27:58,426 --> 00:28:01,303
<i>Me too, you know.
I made some changes when I was there.</i>

517
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:02,972
Yeah. So, like…

518
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:07,602
this time I'll be sure
to make it a success.

519
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:11,480
And I'm thinking I'll… bring home
a cute girlfriend,

520
00:28:11,481 --> 00:28:13,107
so I want you to root for me.

521
00:28:13,108 --> 00:28:15,652
- <i>Isn't that adorable?</i>
- Yeah.

522
00:28:16,569 --> 00:28:20,823
<i>Just do what you think is right,
whatever the result may be.</i>

523
00:28:20,824 --> 00:28:23,785
<i>- Don't be someone that you're not.</i>
- Yeah, you're right.

524
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:27,830
- I'll do it my way. I'll stay true…
- <i>Yeah.</i>

525
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:30,332
- …to myself.
- <i>Okay. Do your best.</i>

526
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:31,459
Mmm, thank you.

527
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:34,420
<i>Well, I'll be cheering for you.</i>

528
00:28:34,421 --> 00:28:36,548
Yeah. I appreciate it.

529
00:28:37,132 --> 00:28:40,843
Next time I see you,
I'll be a more mature version of myself.

530
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,387
<i>That goes for both of us.</i>

531
00:28:42,887 --> 00:28:44,723
<i>- I'll be more mature too.</i>
- Okay.

532
00:28:45,765 --> 00:28:47,349
- <i>Thanks, Tai-chan.</i>
- Same to you.

533
00:28:47,350 --> 00:28:50,395
<i>- Thanks for calling and talking with me.</i>
- Of course. Yeah, see you.

534
00:28:51,146 --> 00:28:53,397
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- Okay, bye-bye.

535
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:54,899
- <i>Okay, good night.</i>
- Night.

536
00:28:56,609 --> 00:28:59,154
<i>He's just adorable--</i>

537
00:29:09,497 --> 00:29:10,665
I'll do my best.

538
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:18,672
- That was Bo Sensei making an appearance…
- Bo!

539
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:20,549
- Bo was so nice.
- …after a long hiatus.

540
00:29:20,550 --> 00:29:23,510
"He's adorable." Beep, beep.

541
00:29:23,511 --> 00:29:24,720
I thought he died or something.

542
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:27,055
He hung up
while he was still talking, right?

543
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:30,517
- Maybe he called because he wanted a push.
- I think you're right. For sure.

544
00:29:30,518 --> 00:29:33,771
- Like, "Okay, I'll do it!"
- He's wavering between two girls.

545
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:35,815
Sharan and Mimi. He can't decide.

546
00:29:36,399 --> 00:29:39,234
- I want him to choose Sharan.
- And Sharan has changed too.

547
00:29:39,235 --> 00:29:41,570
- Yeah.
- She's like a completely different person.

548
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:42,780
- Exactly.
- She's really changed.

549
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:45,032
She told him straight up
that she liked him.

550
00:29:45,033 --> 00:29:48,118
- And as for Rinrin and Kamaken…
- Mmm.

551
00:29:48,119 --> 00:29:49,787
…we actually don't know

552
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:52,289
- if she's gonna say yes to his confession.
- Right, we don't.

553
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:56,418
Because Rinrin seems like,
once her mind is set, her mind is set.

554
00:29:56,419 --> 00:29:58,670
- Yeah.
- She has that tendency, and it shows.

555
00:29:58,671 --> 00:30:01,548
So, unless Kamaken decides
to say something

556
00:30:01,549 --> 00:30:03,842
- or do something impactful…
- Right.

557
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:06,261
…I don't think
he can change Rinrin's mind.

558
00:30:06,262 --> 00:30:09,014
But they're all very straightforward
with their feelings

559
00:30:09,015 --> 00:30:10,557
- during the confession.
- Yeah. Right.

560
00:30:10,558 --> 00:30:14,478
And sometimes, that's when
they finally make up their minds.

561
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:17,356
The words that they choose
to say at the very end

562
00:30:17,357 --> 00:30:19,441
make a huge difference too.

563
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:22,444
BADLY IN LOVE
GRADUATION

564
